  "id": "hawrami_siyah_chamaneh",
  "name": "Siyah-chamaneh and hore (Gurani free-rhythm song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Free-rhythm solo vocal genres of the Gurani-speaking Hawraman highlands on the Iran–Iraq border and of the neighbouring southern Kurdish Kermanshah region. Siyah-chamaneh is sung unaccompanied by a single voice in long, high, melismatic lines on Gurani verse, and hore is an unmetred, deeply ornamented song of lament, longing and devotion sung by singers of the Kermanshah region; both are documented on Kurdish radio and Mahoor field recordings.",
  "recipe": "classic modern siyah-chamaneh and hore, ballad Poetry, med east poetic branch. many notes per syllable, solo unaccompanied, single lead single track no stacking. mountain valley. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
